  "question": {
    "text": "In <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> , let L be a straight line passing through the origin. Suppose that all the points on L are at a constant distance from the two planes <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Let M be the locus of the feet of the perpendiculars drawn from the points on L to the plane <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> . Which of the following points lie (s) on M ?",
    "image": null
  },
